<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>

    <!-- Entitlements for the main app executable (and the bundle signature, which
         is the same Mach-O). Deliberately empty: the Swift binary links DCMTK and
         OpenJPEG statically, loads no third-party dylibs and generates no code at
         runtime, so it needs none of the hardened-runtime exceptions.

         The bundled Python and the plugin venvs run as separate processes, and a
         spawned executable is evaluated against its own signature, not the
         parent's -- so their exceptions live in Python.entitlements and are
         applied only to the binaries under Resources/python/bin.

         App Sandbox (com.apple.security.app-sandbox) is intentionally NOT enabled.
         The app creates a Python venv in ~/Library/Application Support, runs pip
         install, and downloads models from HuggingFace -- all of which require
         unrestricted file system and process execution access that App Sandbox
         does not permit. This means Mac App Store distribution is not possible
         with the current architecture. The sandbox-only keys
         (files.user-selected.*, network.client) have no effect without it and
         are therefore omitted.
         TODO: For future App Store / MDM compatibility, consider pre-bundling all
         Python dependencies and the model inside the app bundle to eliminate
         runtime downloads. -->
</dict>
</plist>
